In article <13300013@m.cs.uiuc.edu>, jfernand@m.cs.uiuc.edu writes:
> > btw, what are the outstanding "bugs" in pl9???
> 3. Exploding a bag on the ground (by #looting instead of applying
> it) causes dungeon collapse.

Also, accidentally putting an empty bag of tricks into your bag of
holding causes an explosion, which somehow caused an EMT trap,
trashing the game.  I'm running PL9 on an AT&T 3B2.

Some other things which may not be bugs, but are at least misfeatures:

- When you stupidly blunder into a pool, you make a last-ditch
	attempt to teleport, and drown if you can't.
	But what if you know how to levitate?
		I lost a good character this way - he'd read his
		spellbook of levitation, and should have been able to
		do that in an emergency, or put on his ring of
		levitation if he had a spare finger.
	Also, jumping boots should let you jump back out.

- jumping boots should let you try to jump into the dark.
	Maybe you should get a warning that a grue might eat you,
	and maybe a grue SHOULD occasionally try to eat you, but you
	should be able to try.  The main place I've wanted this is
	the dark corridor in the castle, to get over the trapdoors.

- The ! and S keys should always work, even at -More- prompts
	or long waits like floating-eye paralysis, fainting, etc.

	Sometimes you need to do something in a hurry, or the
	system is about to go down, or whatever, and you're stuck
	hitting the more key a thousand times while you're sitting
	on Elbereth being cursed at by a herd of kobold shamans.

	It may be hard to get S to work without creating new bugs or
	new ways to cheat, but ! should be relatively clean.

- DEL <or your favorite interrupt key> should allow you to interrupt
	voluntary waits.  Aside from the above-mentioned needs,
	maybe you'd like to stop waiting and kill that orc shaman
	for breakfast, or put on your ring of fire resistance when
	you see that dragon walk in the room just after you typed
	300s, or when the dragon is killing your dog without hitting
	you because you're wearing a ring of conflict, or whatever.

- At there very minimum, it would be nice if voluntary waits and
	searches could be interrupted automatically for hunger
	messages, and optionally for other messages or events.

	This is especially necessary if you've got an old klunky
	keyboard and the keys sometimes stick or the CAPS LOCK is
	unexpectedly set on :-)

- There needs to be some way to kill typeahead; DEL is one option.
	Sometimes your fingers "knew" what was going to happen and
	typed the next dozen moves,

- The ? menu for throwing things should include rocks as well as weapons.
	Throwing other things is unusual enough that they belong on
	the * menu, but rocks are a perfectly normal thing to throw.

- There are a few commands that are redundant; the way they've evolved
	there's no real reason to keep them separate.
	For example, . and s both cause waiting - is there any
		reason you wouldn't want to search while waiting?
	Putting on a ring/amulet/blindfold and Wearing armor are
		similar actions, just as Take-off and Remove are.
		Do they need to be separate?  If you do keep both
		commands, why not let them do either one?

